#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sciences - In brief" tvg-id="961915080" tvg-name="Glaciers are wonders of nature and tourist attractions‚ and they are also the largest reservoirs of drinking water on the planet. In fact‚ 70% of the world's freshwater resources are frozen as snow or ice. These 'water towers' have a major impact on our lives.<br/>From 08.01.2024 13:53" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",42: The Answer to Almost Everything - What Happens When the Glaciers Disappear? (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (08.01.2024)
